C o m p i l a t i o n


      Special-Event Park-and-Ride Planning Problem
      CEE 6410/5410
      David Rosenberg
      October 10, 2026
       
      This problem was contributed by Dr. Ran Sun and expanded by Dr. David Rosenberg
       
      Learning objectives.
      Students will be able to:
      •   Define dimensions, decision variables and an objective function;
      •   Formulate demand, capacity, and service-quality constraints;
      •   Solve a small linear program;
      •   Identify constraints;
       
      Problem Statement
      State Department of Transportation guidance for special events emphasizes advance parklotanning for transportation demand, traffic, parking, transit operations, and seating.
       
      Passengers must also be assigned in full bus-loads of 50 passengers per bus.
       
      Additionally, the event parklotanners must rent and bring in grandstands for the attendees. They have 2 potential venders. Each vender has an up-front reservation cost, number of seats per grandstand, and cost to load, ship, and setup a grandstand.
       
      Vendor  Reservation cost ($)    Seats per grandstand    Cost to load, ship, and setup ($ per grandstand)
      PurpleRain $1,000                   100                 200
      Blue Sky    $1,500                  200                 300
       
      Full details at https://usu.instructure.com/courses/818402/files/100525844?wrap=1
       
      David E Rosenberg
      david.rosenberg@usu.edu
       
      Model Completed By
      Talha Quddoos
      talha.quddoos@usu.edu
      October 09, 2026
       
  38   
  39  * 1. DEFINE the SETS or Dimensions
  40  SETS
  41      i Parking Lots            /north, south, west/
  42      j Vendors of grandstands  /PurpleRain, BlueSky/;
  43   
  44  * 2. DEFINE input data
  45  PARAMETERS
  46     Capacity(i)          Parking lot capacity (each Number is person)                     /north 600,south 500, west  600/
  47     Cost(i)              Cost per passenger from parking lot ($ per person)               /north 4,south 5, west  7/
  48     TravelTime(i)        Travel time from parking lot (minutes)                           /north 20,south 12, west  8/
  49     ReservationCost(j)   Cost to reserve grandstands from vendor ($)                      /PurpleRain 1000, BlueSky    1500/
  50     Seats(j)             Seats per grandstand (number)                                    /PurpleRain 100, BlueSky    200/
  51     UnitCost(j)          Cost per grandstand to load ship and setup ($ per grandstand)    /PurpleRain 200, BlueSky    300/
  52     MaxAverageTime       Maximum average travel time for all pasengers (minutes)          /13/
  53     Attendees            Number of attendees                                              /1200/
  54     BusCapacity          Bus Capacity (Passengers per Bus)                                /50/;
  55   
  56   
  57  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  58  Variables
  59      ECOST    Event Expense ($)
  60      Buses(i) Number of buses from Parking Lot (i)
  61      GS(j)    Number of Grandstands from a Vendor (j)
  62      VSelect(j)     Vendor Selection Binary (1=yes  0=No)
  63   
  64   
  65  ;
  66  Integer Variable Buses, GS;
  67  Binary Variable VSelect;
  68   
  69   
  70  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  71  *EQUATIONS
  72  Equations
  73     Expense         Total Event Cost ($) and obj. function
  74     CapLimit(i)     C: Max capacity of parking space
  75     TTimeLimit      C: Max Avg. Travel Time (mins)
  76     GSLimitSeats    C: Grandstand Limit Seats (Number)
  77     VendorLink(j)   C: Linking Vendor to Binary
  78     RshipLimit      C: All buses ride at capacity
  79  ;
  80   
  81  *Obj Function
  82  Expense..          sum(i,Cost(i)*Buses(i)*BusCapacity)+sum(j,ReservationCost(j)*VSelect(j) + UnitCost(j)* GS(j)) =e=  ECOST ;
  83   
  84  *Constraints
  85  CapLimit(i)..         BusCapacity * Buses(i)                          =l=  Capacity(i) ;
  86  TTimeLimit..          sum(i, TravelTime(i) * Buses(i) * BusCapacity)  =l=  MaxAverageTime*Attendees;
  87  GSLimitSeats..        sum(j, GS(j) * Seats(j))                        =g=  Attendees;
  88  VendorLink(j)..       GS(j)  =l= (Attendees/Seats(j)) * VSelect(j);
  89  RshipLimit..          sum(i, Buses(i) * BusCapacity)                   =g=  Attendees;
  90   
  91  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  92  model EventPlanning /all/;
  93   
  94   
  95  * 6. Solve the Model as a Mixed Integer Program
  96  solve EventPlanning using mip minimize ECOST;
  97   
  98  * 7. Disparklotay the decision variable values in the list file
  99  display GS.L, Buses.L, ECOST.L;
 100   
 101  * Dump all input data and results to a GAMS gdx file
 102  Execute_Unload "MIP-SpecialEvent_Talha.gdx";
 103  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
 104  Execute "gdx2xls MIP-SpecialEvent_Talha.gdx"


